@title EPISODE 21 • WHAT HE DIDN'T SAY
@bg campus_quad_morning
Diggy is waiting outside London's 8 a.m. Two coffees. He looks like he hasn't slept either.
Diggy: Before you say anything — let me say it. All of it. Then you can hate me.
London: Talk.
Diggy: After Family Weekend, my mama's surgery got scheduled. Insurance said no. Your dad heard about it from Coach M. He paid it. The whole thing.
London: And the catch?
Diggy: (long breath) He said, "Focus on your season, son. Let my girls focus on theirs."
London: So you took money to stay away from me.
Diggy: I took money so my mama could walk again. Then I didn't stay away from you. I couldn't.
> [Bitchy] "So I was the price tag. Cute." -> a1
> [Sweet] "...Is your mom okay?" -> a2
> [Bold] "Why didn't you TELL me?" -> a3
> [Bad] Throw the coffee at his feet and walk away. -> a4
*a1
@add Diggy_Trust -2
@add Diggy_Hurt 2
